<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · China, Tibet and Mongolia</p><h1 class="st-title">Northern Wei</h1><p class="st-meta">386 CE – 535 CE · capital Shengle, Pingcheng, Luoyang</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Tuoba Xianbei dynasty that reunified northern China in 439, carved the Yungang and Longmen grottoes and introduced the equal-field system.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-daowu-of-northern-wei">Tuoba Gui</a> restored the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tuoba">Tuoba</a> state of Dai in 386 and soon renamed it Wei. After defeating <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/later-yan">Later Yan</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-canhe-slope">Canhe Slope</a> in 395, he took the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-china-plain">North China Plain</a> and in 398 made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/datong">Pingcheng</a> (Datong) his capital. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-taiwu-of-northern-wei">Emperor Taiwu</a> completed the conquest of the north by taking <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/northern-liang">Northern Liang</a> in 439.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Northern Wei ruled a mostly Chinese population through a <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/xianbei">Xianbei</a> military aristocracy and Chinese officials. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/empress-dowager-feng">Empress Dowager Feng</a> introduced the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/equal-field-system">equal-field</a> system of land allotment in 485. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-xiaowen-of-northern-wei">Emperor Xiaowen</a> moved the capital to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luoyang">Luoyang</a> in 494, banned <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xianbei">Xianbei</a> dress and language at court and adopted the surname Yuan. Despite <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-taiwu-of-northern-wei">Taiwu</a>'s persecution of 446, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buddhism">Buddhism</a> flourished, producing the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yungang-grottoes">Yungang</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/longmen-grottoes">Longmen</a> grottoes.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The Six Garrisons rebellion of 523 by neglected frontier troops shattered the state, and the general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/erzhu-rong">Erzhu Rong</a> massacred the court in 528. In 534 to 535 the dynasty split into <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/eastern-wei">Eastern Wei</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/western-wei">Western Wei</a>, controlled by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gao-huan">Gao Huan</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuwen-tai">Yuwen Tai</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/northern-wei.jpg" alt="Northern Wei" width="320" height="184"><figcaption>Image: Ktrinko · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_of_the_Northern_Wei.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>386 CE – 535 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/4th-century">4th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Shengle, Pingcheng, Luoyang</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Emperor Daowu, Emperor Taiwu, Emperor Xiaowen</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Buddhism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Xianbei, Middle Chinese</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/china">China</a>, <a href="/countries/mongolia">Mongolia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Tuoba Wei, Later Wei</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=460&amp;focus=northern-wei" aria-label="Northern Wei on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7451 936 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Northern Wei lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7771 1192L7205 986M7771 1192L7489 1037M7771 1192L7743 987M7771 1192L7706 1209M7771 1192L7496 1100M7771 1192L7855 1179M7771 1192L7769 1191"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7205 986h0M7489 1037h0M7743 987h0M7706 1209h0M7496 1100h0M7855 1179h0M7769 1191h0"/><path class="map-dot-h